# Production VM deploy (GCP)

**URL:** https://fireplace.ignorelist.com  
**Typical SSH user:** `olek292` (adjust if docs differ).

## Paths (do not guess `~/Fireplace`)

| What | Path |
|------|------|
| Git repo | `~/fireplace` (lowercase) |
| Flutter build output | `~/fireplace/frontend/build/web/` |
| Nginx static root (what users load) | `~/fireplace/frontend-build/` |
| Deploy script (use this one) | `~/fireplace/deploy.sh` |
| Host nginx config | `/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/fireplace` |
| Docker compose project | `~/fireplace/docker-compose.yml` → containers `fireplace-backend-1`, `fireplace-db-1` |

**Wrong:** `cd ~/Fireplace`, running only `~/deploy.sh` from `$HOME` without `cd ~/fireplace` (old 446-byte `~/deploy.sh` copy may lack version dart-defines).

## What `./deploy.sh` does vs does not

**Does:** `git pull` → rebuild **backend** Docker image (with `GIT_COMMIT`, `BUILD_TIME`, `APP_VERSION`) → `flutter build web` into `frontend/build/web/` with **`WEB_PUSH_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`** from `~/fireplace/.env` (must match backend VAPID or PWA push subscribe fails with `push service error` / delivery `400`).

**Does not:** copy web files to `frontend-build/`, reload host nginx, or edit `/etc/nginx/`. Those are separate manual steps on this VM layout.

## Standard deploy (tell user or document after push to `master`)

```bash
cd ~/fireplace
./deploy.sh
cp -a ~/fireplace/frontend/build/web/. ~/fireplace/frontend-build/
curl -sS https://fireplace.ignorelist.com/version
```

Optional: `rsync -a --delete …` if `rsync` installed; `cp -a` is enough.

## Verify production

| Check | Expected |
|-------|----------|
| `curl https://fireplace.ignorelist.com/health` | `{"status":"ok","db":"ok"}` |
| `curl https://fireplace.ignorelist.com/version` | JSON `{ version, gitCommit, buildTime }` — **not** Flutter HTML |
| `curl http://127.0.0.1:3000/version` on VM | Same JSON (backend OK even if nginx broken) |
| App **Settings** footer | `semver · shortSha · buildTime` (e.g. `0.0.2 · 6a560ec · …`; label: App version / Wersja aplikacji) |

If `/version` returns HTML → nginx missing `location = /version` proxy to `127.0.0.1:3000`; fix config, then `sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx`. Template block lives in repo `frontend/nginx.conf` (host uses `127.0.0.1`, not `backend:`).

If Settings shows `· dev` after deploy → PWA/browser cache; hard refresh. Build must use `--dart-define=GIT_COMMIT` (see `deploy.sh`).

## Version fields (do not confuse)

- **Semver in UI/API `version`:** from `frontend/pubspec.yaml` (`0.0.1`, `0.0.2`, … — increment PATCH by 1 per release; never show `+N` suffix).
- **`gitCommit`:** short SHA at deploy time from `git rev-parse` in `deploy.sh`.
- **`buildTime`:** UTC ISO timestamp when deploy ran.

## Nginx / env caveats

- Changing **only** app code: deploy + `cp` enough; no nginx reload.
- Changing **nginx** routes (e.g. new `location`): edit `/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/fireplace`, test, reload.
- **`.env`** in `~/fireplace/.env` is not overwritten by `git pull`; restart backend after env edits. **`WEB_PUSH_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`** in `.env` must match what `deploy.sh` passes to `flutter build web` (script reads it automatically).
- **Postgres on VM:** DB name is **`chatdb`** (not `fireplace`): `docker compose exec db psql -U postgres -d chatdb`.

## Agent checklist after production-related PR

1. User pushed `master` (agent does not SSH unless user asks).
2. Remind full deploy block above if they deploy to VM.
3. Mention new `pubspec` version if bumped.
4. Do not claim prod is updated until user confirms `curl /version` or Settings line.
